...
-	conv_len = smbConvertToUTF16((__le16 *)file_info->FileName, filename,
-				     PATH_MAX, conn->local_nls, 0);
+	conv_len = smbConvertToUTF16((__le16 *)file_info->FileName, filename,
+				     min(filename_len, PATH_MAX),
+				     conn->local_nls, 0);
Reason:
(1) The added check computes the actual free buffer size using smb2_calc_max_out_buf_len() and returns -EINVAL if the required space (2 bytes per character for the filename) exceeds it, preventing the copy when the buffer is too small.
(2) The call to smbConvertToUTF16 is changed from using PATH_MAX to using the actual filename length (clamped by PATH_MAX via min()), ensuring only the necessary bytes are copied and avoiding any potential out-of-bounds write beyond the filename data.

